# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel deployment excludes.
#
# THE IMPORTANT ONE: api/match/ holds the reverse-match NIGHTLY PIPELINE
# (buildMatchTokens.js, runReverseMatch.js, runNightly.js) + the pure scorer
# module (reverseMatch.js). These are NOT HTTP endpoints — they run in GitHub
# Actions (.github/workflows/reverse_match.yml) against the repo checkout, and
# in the `node --test` suite. Vercel otherwise turns every api/**/*.js into a
# Serverless Function; on the Hobby plan the cap is 12, and these 4 pushed the
# count to 13 → "No more than 12 Serverless Functions" build failure.
# Nothing in the deployed runtime imports api/match/* (verified), so excluding
# the directory is safe and drops the function count to 9.
api/match/

# v152 — the SAME failure returned: v151 added api/interview-email.js and
# api/reachout-email.js, taking the count 11 -> 13 and hard-failing every deploy
# with "No more than 12 Serverless Functions ... on the Hobby plan".
#
# api/jobs/ — DEAD in the deployed runtime, and excluding it frees SIX slots:
#   * index.html calls no /api/jobs/* path (verified by grep).
#   * vercel.json's cron pointed at "/api/jobs/index" — a file that does not
#     exist, so that cron has been a daily no-op. Cron removed alongside this.
#   * Jobs are written by the PYTHON harvester (scripts/job_spy_harvester.py via
#     .github/workflows/job_harvest.yml) straight to Firestore. The aggregator
#     path was retired in v45 ("jobs come only from our Firestore harvester").
#   * It could not have run anyway: on Vercel's case-SENSITIVE filesystem
#     require('./atsIngest') and require('./redirectResolver') do not resolve —
#     the real files are Atsingest.js and Redirectresolver.js. Exactly the
#     CLAUDE.md §5 case trap, dormant only because nothing calls it.
# The files stay in the repo (nothing is deleted); they are simply not deployed.
# To bring an endpoint back: delete the line below and FIX THE FILENAME CASE first.
api/jobs/

# vercel.json was also cleaned up alongside this (rationale lives HERE because
# vercel.json's schema is STRICT — it rejects unknown top-level keys, so you cannot
# leave "_comment" notes in it; doing so fails the build with "should NOT have
# additional property"):
#   * the "functions" block for api/jobs/*.js was removed — with the directory
#     excluded the pattern matches zero functions, which Vercel treats as an error,
#     and `memory` is ignored anyway under Active CPU billing.
#   * the daily cron on "/api/jobs/index" was removed — no such file has ever
#     existed, so it resolved to nothing every night. The real harvest is
#     .github/workflows/job_harvest.yml (Python, 05:00 UTC) → Firestore, unaffected.

# api/notifications/ — sendAutomatedEmail.js is a LIBRARY, not an HTTP endpoint:
# it exports { sendAutomatedEmail, sendBatch, ... } with no request handler, and
# no deployed function imports it (verified). Vercel was turning it into a
# function that would 500 if it were ever hit. Frees a 7th slot.
api/notifications/

# Repo assets Vercel never serves or executes — keeps the upload lean.
# NOTE: the GENERATOR is excluded; its OUTPUT (seo/*.html, sitemap.xml, robots.txt)
# is committed and MUST ship — that's the whole point of the static SEO pages.
tests/
docs/
ghost-report-generator/
seo-generator/
scripts/
playwright.config.js
playwright-report/
test-results/
